WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.070
Hey...

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.860
They say it's five centimeters per second.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.410
Huh? What is?

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.040
The speed at which cherry blossoms fall.
It's five centimeters per second.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.330
You sure know a lot of stuff like that, Akari.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.800
Say... don't you think it kinda looks like snow?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.260
I guess...

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.470
Hey! Wait up!

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.100
Akari!

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:46.980
Takaki-kun!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.740
It'd be great if we could watch the cherry
blossoms fall again together next year.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.630
"To Thono Takaki-sama."

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.250
"It's been a really long time."

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.850
"Summer's pretty hot around here,
but compared to Tokyo, it's so much milder."

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.900
"But when I think about it,
I liked Tokyo's hot, humid summers, too."

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.520
"The melting-hot asphalt,"

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.940
"the distant skyscrapers, shimmering in the heat,"

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.450
"and the freezing air-conditioning
in department stores and on subways."

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.330
"The last time we were together was at
our elementary school graduation."

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.330
"It's already been half a year since."

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.160
"So, Takaki-kun..."

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.880
"...do you still remember me?."

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.220
"Dear Takaki-kun..."

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.930
"Thanks for replying."

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.510
"It made me so happy."

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.720
"It's already well into autumn and the
leaves are turning beautiful colors."

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.400
"I had to pull out a sweater the day before
yesterday for the first time this year."

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:10.980
Tohno-kun.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.020
Senpai.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.030
What's that? A love letter?

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.230
That's not it.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.070
Sorry for having asked you to do all that.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.450
No problem, I finished quickly.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.160
Thanks. So, is it true that you'll be transferring schools?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.370
Ah, yes, at the end of the year.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.290
Where to?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.750
Kagoshima. Because of my parents.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.750
I see... it'll be lonely around here without you.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:34.300
"I'm actually writing this letter on the train because
practice has been starting really early lately."

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.590
"I had my hair cut the other day."

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.010
"It's so short you can even see my ears..."

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.350
"...so you probably wouldn't even recognize me
if you saw me."

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:44.140
I'm back.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.180
Welcome home.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:58.990
"I bet you're changing little by little too, Takaki-kun."

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.710
"Dear Takaki-kun..."

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.380
"Have you been doing well during these cold days?"

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.810
"It's already snowed a number of times here."

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.270
"Every time it does, I wrap myself in layers of clothes when I go to school."

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.860
"It hasn't snowed in Tokyo yet, right?."

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.150
"Even though I moved away..."

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.490
"...I still look at Tokyo's weather forecast out of habit."

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.620
Wish it would rain one of these days...

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.620
It wouldn't be any better indoors.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.080
Say... have you guys ever been to Tochigi?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.210
Huh? Where?

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.000
Tochigi.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:53.880
Nope.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.710
I wonder how you get there...

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:56.880
No clue.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.800
A bullet train or something?

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.210
It's a long way...

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.510
Freshmen!

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.140
Yes?!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.430
Onto the final three laps! Fight! Fight!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:13.310
"I was surprised to hear that you were
the one transferring schools this time."

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.360
"We both got used to transferring schools
when we were little.."

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:22.110
"But still... Kagoshima.
That's kind of far away, isn't it?"

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:28.740
"It's no longer a distance where I can just
jump on a train and see you whenever I want..."

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:33.120
"So... I guess... that makes me feel a little lonely."

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.000
"Please be well, Takaki-kun."

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.940
"Dear Takaki-kun..."

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.690
"I'm so happy we'll see each other on March 4th."

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.530
"It'll be just about a year since we last met, won't it?"

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.990
"For some reason, I feel kind of nervous."

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:17.830
"There's a really large cherry tree close to
my house, so I bet that in the spring..."

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.590
"...the petals will fall at five centimeters per second."

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:28.590
"I'm really hoping the spring will come with you that day, Takaki-kun."

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.160
Wanna stop somewhere on the way home?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.780
Well... it's raining out.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.030
The forecast said it's supposed to turn to snow by tonight.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.080
Really? I thought it felt cold.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.000
And we're already in March...

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.580
Yeah, it feels like I'm gonna catch a cold.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.790
We can get off at Shimokita.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.000
Yeah.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.090
Tohno, let's get to practice.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:05.880
Right...

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.680
About that... I don't think I can make it today.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.100
Getting ready to move?

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.060
Something like that.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.890
Sorry.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.600
"I'm glad you're coming all the way out to the station closest to me..."

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.520
"...but it's a long trip, so please be careful."

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:26.150
"I'll be waiting for you in the station's waiting room at 7:00 that night."

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:50.800
<i>On the day Akari and I were to meet,
the rain turned to snow in the afternoon.</i>

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.430
Hey, Takaki-kun.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.480
It's that cat, Chobi.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.850
He's always lying here.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.900
But it looks like he's all by himself today.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.610
What happened to your friend Mimi?
It must be lonely all by yourself, huh?

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:17.870
How's that book so far?

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.160
I really like it.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.670
Last night I read four billion years' worth of evolution.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:22.540
Where are you at now?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.540
Just about when the Anomalocaris start showing up.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.540
The Cambrian era!

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:30.840
I really like the Hallucigenia. They look like this!

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.180
Yeah, something like that...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.800
Which one do you like, Takaki-kun?

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.550
The Opabinia, maybe?

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.640
The five-eyed one, right?

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.810
<i>I think Akari and I were a lot alike somehow.</i>

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.020
<i>Exactly one year after I transferred to Tokyo...</i>

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.440
A new friend just transferred to our school. This is Tohno Takaki-kun.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.400
<i>...Akari transferred into my class.</i>

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.900
Starting today, Shinohara Akari-san will be joining our class.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.700
<i>Because our bodies were still small, frail, and prone to illness...</i>

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.660
<i>...the two of us preferred the library over playing on the sportsfield.</i>

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.950
<i>Naturally, we became friends...</i>

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:03.830
<i>...and because of that, there were times when
our classmates would tease us. But...</i>

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.330
I feel kinda bad for her.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.420
Those two are always together.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.920
Ooh! There he is!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:10.720
<i>As long as we were both together,
strangely, things like that didn't scare us.</i>

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.220
Aw, what a nice guy!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.300
Wow!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.760
<i>And yet, for some reason, I thought we'd
end up going to the same middle school...</i>

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.890
<i>...and stay together, just as we were...</i>

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.190
<i>...from that point on.</i>

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:32.030
Shinjuku, Shinjuku, last stop. For passengers which...

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:38.490
...JR Line, Heiou Line, subway...

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.120
<i>It was the first time I'd gone to Shinjuku Station alone...</i>

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.250
<i>...and all the lines I would soon be riding would also be firsts for me.</i>

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.930
<i>My heart was pounding.</i>

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.390
<i>I was going to see Akari again.</i>

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.690
How did it go with that guy?

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.490
Who?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.150
You know, that Nisshou boy.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.780
Are you kidding? His tastes were a little gross...

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:20.120
We will be arriving at Musashi-Urawa shortly. Again, this is Musashi-Urawa.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.000
At our next stop, Musashi-Urawa, in order to connect with the express train...

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.330
In order to connect with the express train, this train will be stopping for 4 minutes.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:31.250
Those passengers who wish to quickly reach Yonohonmachi and Oomiya please board...

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:56.320
Um... this is Shinohara.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.570
Umm, is Takaki-kun there?

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.530
It's Akari-chan.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.080
Huh? You're transferring schools?

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.170
What about Nishi Middle School?
You went through all that trouble to get accepted.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.630
They said they'd handle the paperwork of transferring
me to the public school in Tochigi...

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:15.460
l'm sorry...

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.510
No... there's no reason to apologize.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:23.140
I told them I still wanted to go from my aunt's house in Katsushika, but...

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:27.020
...they said I couldn't until I was older.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.650
I understand... you don't have to say anything else.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.440
That's enough.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:36.990
I'm sorry...

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.700
<i>Through the receiver painfully pressed against my ear...</i>

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.410
<i>...Akari's own pain was palpable.</i>

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.330
<i>But... there was nothing I could do.</i>

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.210
That was pretty good, huh?

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.210
Yeah. See you later!

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:01.510
<i>The terminal I transferred at was crowded with people heading home...</i>

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.010
<i>...and everyone's shoes were soaked from the snow.</i>

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:10.190
<i>The frigid air was saturated with the classic smell of a snowy city day.</i>

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.350
All passengers, your attention please.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.150
Due to the snowy weather conditions, the Utsunomiya Line
outbound trains traveling to Oomiya and Utsunomiya...

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:19.360
...will be experiencing an 8 minute delay in arrival.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:25.740
We apologize for any inconvenience in your busy day.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:28.410
{i1}Until that moment, I hadn't even considered
the possibility of one of my trains being late.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.960
<i>My creeping anxiety suddenly became much greater.</i>

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:41.050
This train is currently running 10 minutes late due to the snowy weather conditions.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.550
We apologize for any inconvenience in your busy day.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.230
<i>After we had passed a little beyond Oomiya Station...</i>

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.900
<i>...almost all the passing buildings suddenly vanished from view.</i>

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.580
Next stop is Kuki. Kuki.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.540
We apologize for our terribly late arrival.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:18.380
Those passengers transferring to the Tobu Isesaki Line,
please make your way around to Exit #5.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:25.890
Due to the next train's delay, this train will be stopping
at this station for the next 10 minutes.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:32.180
We apologize for any inconvenience in your busy day,
and appreciate your understanding.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.480
Sorry about that.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:40.650
Due to the next train's delay, this train will be stopping
at this station for the next 10 minutes.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:44.820
We apologize for any inconvenience in your busy day, and...

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:08.550
This is Nogi. Nogi.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.220
To all passengers, we express our deepest apologies.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:16.600
Due to the continuing delay of the following train, this train will
be stopping at this station for an extended period of time.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:22.110
We apologize for any inconvenience in your busy day,
and appreciate your understanding.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:22.030
<i>The stations seemed unbelievably far apart...</i>

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:27.320
<i>...and the train would stop for an unbelievably
long amount of time at each station.</i>

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:31.870
Kurihashi > Koga > Nogi > Mamada > Oyama

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:37.040
Omoigawa > Tochigi > Ohirashita > Iwafune > Sano

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:52.430
<i>The wilderness on the other side of the
window seemed like nothing I'd ever experienced before.</i>

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.810
<i>The slowly ticking time...</i>

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.940
<i>...and my pangs of hunger...</i>

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.770
<i>...continued to dampen my spirits.</i>

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.110
<i>The time we had planned to meet had passed...</i>

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.240
<i>...so I had the feeling that Akari was beginning to worry.</i>

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.620
<i>On that day...</i> <i>the day she called...</i>

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.500
<i>On that day...</i> <i>the day she called...</i>

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:24.340
<i>...Akari must've been so much more jittery and upset than me,
yet I couldn't find the words to console her.</i>

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.470
<i>I felt so ashamed of myself.</i>

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:37.680
<i>As we look back, we thank our teachers for all they've done.</i>

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:37.890
Then I guess after today... this is goodbye.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.440
Any summer vacation plans?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.360
<i>I received the first letter from Akari half a year later...</i>

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.070
<i>...during the summer of my first year of middle school.</i>

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.860
<i>I remember every last word of it.</i>

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.950
<i>Over the two weeks before the day we were to meet...</i>

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.790
<i>...I spent my time writing a letter I would give her.</i>

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.460
<i>It was filled with all the things I had to tell her.</i>

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.790
<i>All the things I wanted her to hear.</i>

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.960
<i>There were so many.</i>

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.840
We apologize terribly for the wait.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.550
This train will shortly begin its departure towards Utsunomiya.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.360
This is Oyama. Oyama.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.280
For those passengers changing over to the
Tohoku Bullet Train, please transfer here.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:32.910
Those passengers transferring to the down-train,
the Tohoku Bullet Train towards Morioka, please transfer to Line 1.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:37.490
Those passengers transferring to the up-train
towards Tokyo, please transfer to Line 5.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:40.580
Those passengers transferring to the Mito Line-

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.580
All passengers, your attention please.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:46.340
Due to snowy weather conditions, the
Ryomo Line is currently experiencing a serious delay.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:50.090
We apologize for the terrible inconvenience.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:53.760
We ask that you please be patient and wait a little longer until the train arrives.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.760
The next up-train headed for--

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.060
<i>Either way...</i>

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:01.350
<i>...I had no choice but to keep going towards
the station where Akari was waiting.</i>

00:16:55.450 --> 00:17:00.580
This is the up-train, Line 8, towards Takasaki,
passing Ashikaga and Maebashi on the way.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.790
Please stand behind the white line--

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.740
All passengers, your attention please.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:41.740
Due to the disrupted schedule from the heavy snowfall
this train will be making a temporary stop.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.200
We apologize terribly for this inconvenience in your busy day...

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.790
...but presently, we are unable to resume normal service.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.790
I repeat...

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:03.970
"Dear Takaki-kun..."

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.520
"How are you?"

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:10.730
"I'm actually writing this letter on the train because
practice has been starting really early lately."

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.190
<i>Every time I tried to picture Akari from her letters...</i>

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:16.280
<i>...she was always alone for some reason.</i>

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:26.290
<i>In the end, the train remained stopped
in the barren wilderness for two hours.</i>

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.130
<i>Each minute felt like an eternity.</i>

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.790
<i>With clear malice towards me...</i>

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:36.300
<i>...time continued to drift slowly forwards around me.</i>

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.890
<i>I clenched my teeth tightly together...</i>

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:44.310
<i>...and could do nothing but endure the pain and hold back my tears.</i>

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.310
<i>Akari....</i>

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.480
<i>Please tell me...</i>

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.650
<i>...you've already...</i>

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.780
<i>...returned home.</i>

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:16.050
Line 3 towards Takasaki, passing Ashikaga
and Maebashi on the way has just arrived.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.590
Due to the snowy weather conditions, this train
will be making a temporary stop.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.880
Akari....

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.000
It tastes good.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.620
Really?

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.290
It's just hot roasted tea.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.500
Roasted tea?

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.170
This is my first time having it...

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:39.630
You're kidding. I'm sure you've had it before.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.630
You think?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.720
You must have.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:47.800
And... since I made this, I can't really guarantee how good it'll taste, but...

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.390
If you'd like, please have some.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.850
Thanks!

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:54.900
I was really hungry.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:20:59.650
How is it?

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.820
It's the most delicious rice ball I've ever had.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:08.660
You're exaggerating!

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:09.660
It really is!

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.540
It's probably just because you're hungry.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:12.500
You think so?

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.710
It must be.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.420
I think I'll have a bite, too.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.760
So... you're moving soon, right?

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.300
Yeah. Next week.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:25.840
Kagoshima, huh?

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.890
It's pretty far away.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:27.550
Yeah...

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:31.010
Though this trip to Tochigi was pretty far, too.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.770
You can't even go home today now, after all.

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:39.310
We'll be closing soon. There aren't any more trains coming or going.

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.480
Yes, sir.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.650
Be careful on your way home in this snow.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:43.440
Yes, sir.

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.340
Can you see the tree way out there?

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.050
Is that the tree from your letters?

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:13.140
Yeah. It's a cherry tree.

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:21.360
So...

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:25.070
...don't you think it looks a little like snow?

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:33.910
It sure does.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:45.840
<i>In that moment...</i>

00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:51.970
<i>...I felt like I knew where eternity, our hearts and ours souls all lay.</i>

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:56.980
<i>I felt as though we had shared
all the experiences of my 13 years.<i></i></i>

00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:59.770
<i>And then... in the next moment...</i>

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:02.940
<i>...I was suddenly filled with an insufferable sadness.</i>

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:08.240
<i>Akari's warmth... and her soul...</i>

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:12.570
<i>How could I take them in, and where could I bring them?</i>

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:15.240
<i>I felt that sad because I didn't have those answers.</i>

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.590
<i>I clearly knew that from that point on, we wouldn't be together forever.</i>

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:27.420
<i>The overwhelming weight of our lives to come...</i>

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:32.300
<i>...and the uncertainty of time hung over us.<i></i></i>

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.640
<i>But... the creeping anxiety that had taken hold of me...</i>

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:39.020
<i>But... the creeping anxiety that had taken hold of me...</i>

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:41.520
<i>...would soon gradually melt away.</i>

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:46.440
<i>And all that remained would be the feeling of Akari's soft lips.</i>

00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:09.670
<i>We spent that night in a shack by the side of a field.</i>

00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:15.300
<i>Wrapping ourselves in an old blanket, we talked on and on...</i>

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:17.970
<i>...until finally, we had fallen asleep, side by side.</i>

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:22.310
<i>The next morning, as I boarded the train that had started its run again...</i>

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:24.560
<i>...I parted with Akari..</i>

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:30.150
Umm... Takaki-kun...

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:30.940
Yeah?

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:33.990
Takaki-kun...

00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:37.780
...I'm sure you'll be okay from now on.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:38.540
I just know it!

00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:39.990
Thank you.

00:24:41.500 --> 00:24:42.830
Akari, you be well, too!

00:24:43.580 --> 00:24:44.540
I'll write you!

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:45.330
I'll call, too!

00:24:58.680 --> 00:25:03.640
<i>I never told Akari that I'd lost the letter I wanted to give her.</i>

00:25:05.810 --> 00:25:12.990
<i>Because I felt that my world had completely changed after that kiss.</i>

00:25:20.790 --> 00:25:25.370
<i>All I wanted was the strength to protect her.</i>

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:33.380
<i>With that thought in my mind, I continued to gaze out
over the landscape beyond the window... forever.</i>

00:25:33.920 --> 00:25:47.400
End

00:25:34.010 --> 00:25:47.480
Episode 1    Cherry Blossom

00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:03.890
Kanae, are you going to go after school, too?

00:27:03.890 --> 00:27:05.680
Yeah, are you okay with that, Onee-chan?

00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:08.140
Fine by me. But be sure to get to your studies, too.

00:27:08.140 --> 00:27:09.270
Yeah.

00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:40.340
Okay!

00:27:55.060 --> 00:27:56.020
Morning.

00:27:56.520 --> 00:27:58.280
Good morning, Tohno-kun.

00:27:58.280 --> 00:27:59.740
You're really early this morning, huh?

00:27:59.740 --> 00:28:02.110
You too, Sumida. You went to the beach again, right?

00:28:02.110 --> 00:28:02.780
Yeah.

00:28:03.410 --> 00:28:05.030
You're practicing hard.

00:28:06.120 --> 00:28:08.830
I wouldn't say that...

00:28:08.830 --> 00:28:10.500
See you later, Tohno-kun.

00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:11.210
Later.

00:28:13.790 --> 00:28:16.460
Got it? It's time to begin making your choices.

00:28:16.460 --> 00:28:18.630
Be sure to turn it in by Monday, okay?

00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:21.170
And remember to talk it over with your parents before.

00:28:22.970 --> 00:28:26.140
Looks like Sasaki-san's gonna be going to a college in Tokyo.

00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:29.850
No surprise there. I was thinking of maybe
going to a 2-year college in Kumamoto.

00:28:29.850 --> 00:28:31.180
What about you, Kanae?

00:28:31.180 --> 00:28:33.480
Huh? Umm...

00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:34.900
Will you get a job?

00:28:34.900 --> 00:28:36.310
Umm...

00:28:36.310 --> 00:28:38.860
You really haven't thought about it at all, huh?

00:28:38.860 --> 00:28:40.530
The only thing on your mind is Tohno-kun, right?

00:28:40.530 --> 00:28:42.900
He definitely left his girlfriend in Tokyo, I'm telling you.

00:28:42.900 --> 00:28:44.200
No way!

00:29:11.720 --> 00:29:13.600
Still not going well for you?

00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:15.770
Yeah... what's gotten into me?

00:29:16.650 --> 00:29:20.820
It's better if you don't think about it too much.
You'll be able to surf again in no time, I promise.

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:22.860
It must be nice taking things so easy, Onee-chan.

00:29:22.860 --> 00:29:24.650
What are you in such a rush for?

00:29:26.570 --> 00:29:30.410
At this rate, I won't be able to say it before graduation...

00:29:48.970 --> 00:29:50.680
Thanks, Onee-chan.

00:29:50.680 --> 00:29:51.810
I can take you home, too...

00:29:51.810 --> 00:29:54.020
Don't worry about it. I'll take my bike home.

00:30:21.670 --> 00:30:23.420
Sumida, you're on your way home?

00:30:23.420 --> 00:30:24.260
Yeah.

00:30:24.710 --> 00:30:25.670
You too, Tohno-kun?

00:30:25.670 --> 00:30:26.470
Yeah.

00:30:27.010 --> 00:30:28.300
Wanna go home together?

00:30:29.300 --> 00:30:32.050
<i>If I had a tail like a dog's...</i>

00:30:32.430 --> 00:30:36.600
<i>...I'm sure it'd be wagging back and forth right now,
since I'd be unable to hide my happiness.</i>

00:30:37.230 --> 00:30:42.320
<i>I was sort of relieved and thought to myself,
"Thank goodness I'm not really a dog..."</i>

00:30:42.320 --> 00:30:46.190
<i>...and I was surprised at how foolish I was for thinking what I did earlier.</i>

00:30:46.190 --> 00:30:50.360
<i>But even still, the trip home with Tohno-kun was bliss.</i>

00:30:53.530 --> 00:30:59.290
{i1}Right from the start, Tohno-kun seemed
a little different from the other boys.

00:31:00.330 --> 00:31:01.670
I'm Tohno Takaki.

00:31:01.670 --> 00:31:04.420
I'm sorta used to transferring schools because of my parents' jobs...

00:31:04.420 --> 00:31:06.460
...but I'm not too used to this island yet.

00:31:06.590 --> 00:31:08.090
It's nice to meet you all.

00:31:08.090 --> 00:31:12.720
<i>I fell in love at first sight on that day in the second year of middle
school, and wanted to go to the same high school as him...</i>

00:31:13.050 --> 00:31:16.270
<i>...so I studied really hard, was somehow accepted...</i>

00:31:16.270 --> 00:31:21.730
<i>...and every single time I saw him, fell more and more in love with him.</i>

00:31:21.730 --> 00:31:24.900
<i>But it's so scary, and everyday is painful.</i>

00:31:24.900 --> 00:31:27.190
<i>Yet every time I see him, I'm filled with such happiness...</i>

00:31:27.190 --> 00:31:30.070
<i>...that I'm at a loss for what to do.</i>

00:31:31.700 --> 00:31:33.870
Tohno-kun, there you go buying the same one again.

00:31:34.280 --> 00:31:35.620
It's really good.

00:31:36.120 --> 00:31:39.460
Sumida, you always think your decisions
through seriously, don't you?

00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:40.330
Yeah.

00:31:42.670 --> 00:31:43.880
I'll be outside.

00:31:44.460 --> 00:31:45.250
Yeah.

00:31:45.960 --> 00:31:47.050
Just this, please.

00:31:47.050 --> 00:31:48.760
That'll be 90 yen.

00:31:48.970 --> 00:31:49.760
Here you go.

00:31:49.760 --> 00:31:51.090
Thanks as always.

00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:03.020
Welcome back.

00:32:03.020 --> 00:32:04.110
What'd you buy?

00:32:04.110 --> 00:32:07.690
Well, it was hard to pick, but I went with this.

00:32:05.480 --> 00:32:09.070
<i>Sometimes, Tohno-kun would be writing a text message...</i>

00:32:09.070 --> 00:32:10.740
<i>...and every time he did, I would always wish...</i>

00:32:10.740 --> 00:32:13.570
<i>...that the text message he was writing...</i>

00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:18.080
<i>...would be addressed to me.</i>

00:32:27.840 --> 00:32:29.210
Kabu, I'm home!

00:32:29.210 --> 00:32:30.800
Kabu, Kabu!

00:32:30.800 --> 00:32:32.220
I'm back.

00:32:52.650 --> 00:32:54.990
This is a message from your town hall.

00:32:54.990 --> 00:32:58.120
The next normal open gasoline stand will be at the
Sakai Agricultural Cooperative Gas Station.

00:32:58.120 --> 00:33:00.910
Sumida Kanae-san from Class 3-1...

00:33:00.910 --> 00:33:02.710
...Itou-sensei is calling for you.

00:33:02.710 --> 00:33:04.500
Please report to the Guidance Counselor's office.

00:33:03.960 --> 00:33:05.580
Oh, that's your girlfriend.

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:07.340
She's not my girlfriend.

00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:13.590
You're the only one in the grade who hasn't filled one out.

00:33:13.590 --> 00:33:14.930
I'm sorry.

00:33:14.930 --> 00:33:17.970
Look, this isn't something someone in my position should be saying...

00:33:17.970 --> 00:33:20.430
...but this isn't really something you have to wrack your brain over.

00:33:20.430 --> 00:33:22.600
Has Sumida-sensei said anything?

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:23.770
No...

00:33:26.440 --> 00:33:30.400
If you really can't decide, then how about
a 2-year college within the prefecture?

00:33:30.400 --> 00:33:31.360
But...

00:33:33.400 --> 00:33:35.780
<i>Onee-chan has nothing to do with it...</i>

00:33:53.590 --> 00:33:54.550
<i>After all...</i>

00:33:56.380 --> 00:33:59.220
<i>...surfing, even after I pestered my sister so much to teach me...</i>

00:33:59.220 --> 00:34:02.520
<i>...and the most important guy who takes up all of my thoughts...</i>

00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:05.770
<i>...are two things I'm still no good at.</i>

00:34:31.090 --> 00:34:32.670
Thanks as always.

00:34:32.670 --> 00:34:34.010
Not at all. See you next time.

00:34:34.010 --> 00:34:35.630
Not at all. See you next time.

00:35:03.870 --> 00:35:06.330
<i>Whenever I go to where Tohno-kun is...</i>

00:35:06.330 --> 00:35:10.120
<i>...deep down, my heart... it clenches up... just a little.</i>

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:11.880
Tohno-kun.

00:35:11.880 --> 00:35:14.920
Sumida, what's up? I'm surprised you found me way out here.

00:35:16.010 --> 00:35:19.340
I saw your bike, so I decided to come on by.

00:35:19.340 --> 00:35:19.930
That okay?

00:35:19.930 --> 00:35:22.090
Ah, I see. I'm glad to see you.

00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:25.390
We didn't run into each other at the bike shed today.

00:35:25.390 --> 00:35:26.680
I'm glad, too.

00:35:26.890 --> 00:35:28.270
<i>He's really kind.</i>

00:35:28.980 --> 00:35:32.980
<i>So kind that sometimes it feels like I'm going to cry.</i>

00:35:35.230 --> 00:35:37.320
Hey, are you going to test to get into college?

00:35:37.320 --> 00:35:40.240
Yeah. I'm going to take a few for some universities in Tokyo.

00:35:40.240 --> 00:35:41.990
Tokyo... I see.

00:35:41.990 --> 00:35:43.160
Tokyo... I see.

00:35:43.160 --> 00:35:44.870
I thought that might be the case.

00:35:45.660 --> 00:35:46.740
Why do you say that?

00:35:46.740 --> 00:35:49.830
You seem like you want to go far away from here, for some reason...

00:35:50.410 --> 00:35:51.620
What about you, Sumida?

00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:56.420
I don't even really know what's going to happen tomorrow.

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:58.380
Everyone's the same.

00:35:58.380 --> 00:36:00.380
No way! You too, Tohno-kun?

00:36:00.380 --> 00:36:01.300
Of course.

00:36:02.180 --> 00:36:05.010
You don't look like you have anything to worry about.

00:36:05.010 --> 00:36:08.310
Oh, stop that. I'm filled with nothing but worries.

00:36:08.310 --> 00:36:11.940
I'm doing all that I can just to keep up. I have no breathing room.

00:36:12.600 --> 00:36:13.650
Really?

00:36:14.770 --> 00:36:16.020
I see...

00:36:23.530 --> 00:36:24.870
A plane?

00:36:24.870 --> 00:36:25.620
Yeah.

00:37:16.170 --> 00:37:17.170
Wow...

00:37:18.540 --> 00:37:20.340
They say it travels at five kilometers per hour.

00:37:22.130 --> 00:37:24.300
It's going to the Minamitane launch facility.

00:37:25.550 --> 00:37:28.640
Looks like there'll be a launch this year. First time in a while.

00:37:28.640 --> 00:37:32.220
Yeah. It's supposed to go to the far reaches of the solar system.

00:37:32.220 --> 00:37:33.890
No matter how many years it takes...

00:37:53.120 --> 00:37:57.080
Hey... you should really talk to Kanae about her plans for the future.

00:37:57.080 --> 00:37:58.920
You know how absent-minded she can be.

00:37:58.920 --> 00:38:02.300
She'll be fine. It's not like she's a child anymore.

00:38:06.180 --> 00:38:08.300
I remember when I used to be just like that, a long time ago...

00:38:10.180 --> 00:38:14.350
Hear that, Kabu? Tohno-kun apparently doesn't
know what tomorrow will bring, either.

00:38:14.350 --> 00:38:16.810
We're both the same. Tohno-kun and me.

00:38:17.940 --> 00:38:20.060
<i>It must really be...</i>

00:38:20.770 --> 00:38:24.240
<i>...a lonelier journey than anyone could imagine.</i>

00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:28.700
<i>To just press forward through the true pitch darkness...</i>

00:38:28.700 --> 00:38:31.830
<i>Barely encountering even a single hydrogen atom...</i>

00:38:33.040 --> 00:38:35.660
<i>Wholeheartedly believing you'll come closer to discovering...</i>

00:38:35.660 --> 00:38:38.870
<i>...the secrets of the universe within the unfathomable abyss of space.</i>

00:38:43.920 --> 00:38:47.380
<i>I wonder how far we should go...</i>

00:38:48.180 --> 00:38:50.510
<i>How far </i>can<i> we go?</i>

00:39:09.860 --> 00:39:14.330
<i>I wonder when I got in the habit of
writing messages to nobody?</i>

00:39:51.660 --> 00:39:54.120
Kanae, have you decided what you'll be doing in the future?

00:39:54.120 --> 00:39:56.830
Nope. Like I thought, I'm still not sure...

00:39:56.830 --> 00:40:01.580
But it's all right! I decided that I'll just take things on one at a time.

00:40:01.580 --> 00:40:02.500
Off I go!

00:40:20.140 --> 00:40:24.020
<i>Since that day, a number of typhoons have passed through...</i>

00:40:24.310 --> 00:40:27.940
<i>...and the island's become a little cooler each time.</i>

00:40:29.940 --> 00:40:33.410
<i>The wind blowing through the sugarcane has taken on a slight chill...</i>

00:40:33.410 --> 00:40:35.700
<i>...and the sky seems a little higher.</i>

00:40:35.700 --> 00:40:38.240
<i>The edges of the clouds have become gentler...</i>

00:40:38.240 --> 00:40:43.080
<i>...and my classmates have begun wearing light jackets
when riding their bikes with the change in the weather.</i>

00:40:58.180 --> 00:41:01.640
<i>By the time I managed to ride the waves again,
six long months had passed.</i>

00:41:01.640 --> 00:41:07.060
<i>Even though it was the middle of October, it felt
like a little bit of summer had been left behind.</i>

00:41:17.160 --> 00:41:22.330
The weather forecast for tonight shows a clear evening
with winds up to eight meters per second.

00:41:21.790 --> 00:41:25.080
So I heard that Yamada confessed to Sasaki-san.

00:41:25.080 --> 00:41:26.580
No surprise there.

00:41:26.920 --> 00:41:29.460
Huh? Kanae, you seem awfully happy today.

00:41:29.460 --> 00:41:31.460
Something good happen between you and Tohno-kun?

00:41:32.840 --> 00:41:33.760
No way!

00:41:35.430 --> 00:41:39.430
<i>Today, I'm finally going to confess to Tohno-kun, too.</i>

00:41:44.640 --> 00:41:46.980
<i>If I don't tell him today, on the day I finally rode the waves again...</i>

00:41:46.980 --> 00:41:49.860
{i1}...I'm sure l won't ever be able to.

00:42:00.450 --> 00:42:01.580
Sumida.

00:42:01.580 --> 00:42:02.290
To—

00:42:03.660 --> 00:42:04.830
Tohno-kun.

00:42:05.290 --> 00:42:06.080
On your way home?

00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:06.790
Yeah.

00:42:07.370 --> 00:42:08.170
I see.

00:42:08.170 --> 00:42:10.250
Then, let's go home together.

00:42:32.980 --> 00:42:35.570
Huh, Sumida? Decided already today?

00:42:35.570 --> 00:42:36.320
Yeah.

00:42:47.750 --> 00:42:48.460
What's the matter?

00:42:55.960 --> 00:42:57.260
...to me...

00:42:59.840 --> 00:43:01.260
No... I'm sorry. It's nothing.

00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:03.140
No... I'm sorry. It's nothing.

00:43:11.440 --> 00:43:12.730
Is your bike acting up?

00:43:12.730 --> 00:43:14.690
Yeah... that's kind of weird.

00:43:16.150 --> 00:43:17.030
Is it broken?

00:43:17.030 --> 00:43:20.160
Yeah... I think the spark plug's dead.

00:43:20.570 --> 00:43:21.740
Was this a hand-me-down?

00:43:21.740 --> 00:43:23.120
Yeah. It was Onee-chan's.

00:43:23.120 --> 00:43:24.910
Did it stall when you tried accelerating?

00:43:24.910 --> 00:43:26.410
It might have, actually...

00:43:27.370 --> 00:43:29.370
Let's leave it here for today.

00:43:29.370 --> 00:43:32.000
You can have someone from your house pick it up later.

00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:33.290
Let's walk back today.

00:43:33.290 --> 00:43:35.710
Huh? I'll walk by myself!

00:43:35.710 --> 00:43:37.550
You go on ahead.

00:43:37.550 --> 00:43:39.630
We're far out and your place is nearby.

00:43:39.630 --> 00:43:42.260
And... I kind of want to walk today.

00:44:17.960 --> 00:44:20.670
<i>Tohno-kun, please...</i>

00:44:31.770 --> 00:44:32.640
What's wrong?

00:44:32.640 --> 00:44:33.810
I'm sorry...

00:44:34.650 --> 00:44:36.020
It's nothing.

00:44:36.020 --> 00:44:36.980
I'm so sorry...

00:44:39.610 --> 00:44:40.570
Sumida...

00:44:42.740 --> 00:44:45.530
<i>I'm begging you... please...</i>

00:44:45.530 --> 00:44:49.040
<i>...don't be so nice to me!</i>

00:46:23.710 --> 00:46:27.840
<i>As we humans desperately and recklessly
stretched our arms to the top of the sky...</i>

00:46:27.840 --> 00:46:30.850
<i>...and launched something of that mass and size into the air...</i>

00:46:30.850 --> 00:46:34.560
<i>...gazing off into the distance towards something
far beyond our wildest dreams...</i>

00:46:39.520 --> 00:46:45.610
<i>...I felt like I somewhat came to understand why
Tohno-kun was different from the other boys.</i>

00:46:45.610 --> 00:46:47.530
<i>And at the same time... I clearly realized that Tohno-kun wasn't really looking at me.</i>

00:46:47.530 --> 00:46:53.700
<i>And at the same time... I clearly realized that Tohno-kun wasn't really looking at me.</i>

00:46:57.910 --> 00:47:02.340
<i>Which is why, on that day, I couldn't say a word to Tohno-kun.</i>

00:47:16.180 --> 00:47:18.520
<i>Tohno-kun is really kind, but...</i>

00:47:18.520 --> 00:47:20.650
<i>He's so truly kind, but...</i>

00:47:22.110 --> 00:47:26.740
<i>But Tohno-kun was always looking far beyond me.</i>

00:47:26.740 --> 00:47:30.280
<i>Far beyond me, towards something in the distance.</i>

00:47:40.250 --> 00:47:44.090
<i>I'm sure I wouldn't be able to give Tohno-kun what he truly desires.</i>

00:47:44.540 --> 00:47:48.050
<i>But still... despite that...</i>

00:47:48.050 --> 00:47:51.640
<i>Tomorrow, the day after, and even beyond that...</i>

00:47:51.640 --> 00:47:54.430
<i>...I know I'll still be helplessly in love with him.</i>

00:47:57.100 --> 00:48:02.940
<i>While thinking solely of Tohno-kun, I cried myself to sleep.</i>

00:49:29.480 --> 00:49:31.820
<i>I strongly felt...</i>

00:49:31.820 --> 00:49:33.740
<i>...that if I looked back now...</i>

00:49:33.740 --> 00:49:35.820
<i>...she would look back as well.</i>

00:49:49.380 --> 00:49:53.630
The last Chuo line train bound for Tokyo is now arriving.

00:51:09.670 --> 00:51:11.750
You should stay till New Year's.

00:51:11.750 --> 00:51:14.920
I know, but I have a million things to take care of.

00:51:14.920 --> 00:51:16.380
I guess so.

00:51:16.380 --> 00:51:18.590
Be sure to cook him good meals, you hear?

00:51:18.590 --> 00:51:19.300
I will.

00:51:19.300 --> 00:51:22.430
If there's ever a problem, don't hesitate to call us, Akari.

00:51:22.430 --> 00:51:23.680
I'll be fine.

00:51:23.680 --> 00:51:27.100
We'll see each other at the wedding next month, so don't worry so much.

00:51:27.100 --> 00:51:30.230
The train for platform 2 is now arriving.

00:51:27.850 --> 00:51:29.940
You'd better head home. It's cold.

00:51:50.290 --> 00:51:53.460
<i>Last night, I dreamt of something from the distant past.</i>

00:51:54.710 --> 00:51:58.170
<i>Back when he and I were both still children.</i>

00:51:58.670 --> 00:52:01.930
<i>I'm sure it's because of that letter I found yesterday.</i>

00:52:55.690 --> 00:52:56.400
Mizuno-san.

00:52:56.400 --> 00:52:57.570
Ah, yes, sir?

00:52:57.570 --> 00:52:58.650
Have time for that meeting?

00:52:58.650 --> 00:52:59.610
Yes, sir.

00:53:08.240 --> 00:53:13.460
<i>Through the act of living itself, sadness piles up here and there.</i>

00:53:14.500 --> 00:53:16.630
<i>Whether in the sheets hung to dry in the sun...</i>

00:53:16.630 --> 00:53:18.340
<i>...the single toothbrush in your bathroom...</i>

00:53:18.340 --> 00:53:20.880
<i>...or the history logs of your cell phone.</i>

00:53:43.030 --> 00:53:46.160
<i>"Even now, I still love you..."</i>

00:53:46.160 --> 00:53:50.700
<i>That's what the girl I'd been with for three years
said in that e-mail.</i>

00:53:51.160 --> 00:53:55.920
<i>"But I'm sure that even if we had written
1,000 text messages back and forth..."</i>

00:53:55.920 --> 00:54:00.210
<i>"...our hearts probably wouldn't have moved even 1 centimeter closer."</i>

00:54:08.720 --> 00:54:14.810
<i>Over these past few years, I've only wanted to move
forward and touch that which I couldn't reach...</i>

00:54:14.810 --> 00:54:17.060
<i>...though I've never been able to tangibly define what it was.</i>

00:54:17.060 --> 00:54:24.610
<i>Not knowing where those obsessive thoughts
came from, I simply continued to work.</i>

00:54:24.610 --> 00:54:29.280
<i>Then one day I realized that my heart was withering,
and in it there was nothing but pain.</i>

00:54:30.910 --> 00:54:32.910
<i>And then, one morning...</i>

00:54:32.910 --> 00:54:38.750
<i>...when I realized that I had completely lost my
earnest and acute feelings from long ago...</i>

00:54:39.330 --> 00:54:41.670
<i>...I knew I was at my limit...</i>

00:54:41.670 --> 00:54:43.420
<i>...and quit my job.</i>

00:55:09.240 --> 00:55:11.740
<i>Yesterday, I had a dream.</i>

00:55:11.740 --> 00:55:13.990
<i>A dream of long ago.</i>

00:55:14.410 --> 00:55:18.370
<i>Within the dream, the two of us were still thirteen...</i>

00:55:18.370 --> 00:55:22.750
<i>...standing upon the vast field blanketed
in snow as far as the eye could see.</i>

00:55:22.750 --> 00:55:27.010
<i>In the distance, the lights shimmering in
houses were set sparsely, far and wide.</i>

00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:32.430
<i>All that was left upon the newly fallen snow were our footprints.</i>

00:55:32.430 --> 00:55:33.930
<i>Just like that...</i>

00:55:33.930 --> 00:55:37.430
<i>...we wished, without hesitation, that one day...</i>

00:55:37.430 --> 00:55:39.270
<i>...the two of us would be able...</i>

00:55:39.270 --> 00:55:40.940
<i>...to see the cherry blossoms together again.</i>

00:55:40.940 --> 00:55:42.520
<i>...to see the cherry blossoms together again.</i>
